=== stdout ===
OVERVIEW: Open a crash's source location in Xcode via xed.

Examples:
  xcrashlytics open FB-3aedb610eee1a41872d991ca62ce8566
  xcrashlytics open FB-3aedb610eee1a41872d991ca62ce8566/events/E1
  xcrashlytics open XC-AAAAAAAA-BBBB-CCCC-DDDD-EEEEEEEEEEEE

Crash frames carry file names only, so the file is resolved inside the current
directory — run from the app's repo root.

USAGE: xcrashlytics open <id> [--crash-directory <crash-directory> ...]

ARGUMENTS:
  <id>                    Crash id (XC-<uuid> or FB-<id>).

OPTIONS:
  --crash-directory <crash-directory>
                          XC- ids: Xcode crash directory to scan instead of the
                          profile's Organizer directories. Repeatable.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

